1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
New brakes squeaking?

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
That's not always bad news.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Fresh pads leave a thin
resin layer on the rotor —

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
that's usually what you're hearing.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,200
A proper bed-in — a few hard
stops from speed, no full stop —

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,000
burns that glaze off evenly.

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,200
Still squeaking two or
three weeks later?

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,000
That's worth a second look,
not just glaze.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,800
New brakes won't quit squeaking?
Send us a message, we'll take a listen.

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,000
Nick's Tire and Auto — link in bio.
